    "created_at": "2018-11-28T13:27:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-11-28T16:01:15Z",
    "body": "Yeah, I know, but I feel like this isn't one of them.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure that the ordinal value of a list item is a \"rendering thing\", particularly in an ordered list. And the text contents of an `li::marker` node seems like it should also be available, even if that strictly speaking is the result of rendering. (But I'm fine with treating these two points as independent—this ticket is primarily about exposing the ordinal value of a list item to scripting.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
